1
00:00:02,211 --> 00:00:04,935
So now we also have the NotFound error

2
00:00:04,983 --> 00:00:07,948
handling. To now really conclude this basics

3
00:00:07,948 --> 00:00:08,557
module here,

4
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:10,800
let's work on our code structure.

5
00:00:11,409 --> 00:00:13,781
This is a simple app and having it all in

6
00:00:13,877 --> 00:00:15,784
one file is perfectly fine.

7
00:00:16,457 --> 00:00:18,220
But typically you're going to build bigger

8
00:00:18,284 --> 00:00:20,399
apps than that and therefore you might wanna

9
00:00:20,399 --> 00:00:23,396
split your code across multiple files to

10
00:00:23,428 --> 00:00:26,282
keep every file on its own, small and

11
00:00:26,394 --> 00:00:28,946
manageable so that it's easy to find what

12
00:00:28,946 --> 00:00:30,551
you're looking for and you don't have to

13
00:00:30,551 --> 00:00:32,814
scroll through super long files all the

14
00:00:32,814 --> 00:00:33,119
time.

15
00:00:34,018 --> 00:00:36,554
And for that, a common folder structure in

16
00:00:36,827 --> 00:00:39,844
Node and therefore also in Deno projects is

17
00:00:39,892 --> 00:00:43,102
that we have a separate folder named routes

18
00:00:43,231 --> 00:00:45,157
or router— the name is up to you—

19
00:00:45,734 --> 00:00:47,917
which will hold your routing logic.

20
00:00:48,688 --> 00:00:50,999
And here I'll add my goals.ts file

21
00:00:51,577 --> 00:00:53,053
and move my router here

22
00:00:54,225 --> 00:00:56,183
and the routes which I configure on it

23
00:00:57,194 --> 00:00:58,686
out of the app.ts file

24
00:00:59,280 --> 00:01:00,677
into that goals.ts file.

25
00:01:01,945 --> 00:01:03,566
That of course means that we also

26
00:01:04,496 --> 00:01:07,594
need to copy that import, remove the router

27
00:01:07,722 --> 00:01:08,814
import in app.ts,

28
00:01:09,648 --> 00:01:11,430
and instead here in goals.ts

29
00:01:11,959 --> 00:01:12,778
add the router.

30
00:01:14,126 --> 00:01:16,550
Don't import the rest, but add the router

31
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:17,737
import from from Oak.

32
00:01:18,636 --> 00:01:20,594
And of course, since I'm now rendering my

33
00:01:20,642 --> 00:01:21,316
templates here,

34
00:01:22,006 --> 00:01:25,648
I also want to import renderFileToString not

35
00:01:25,696 --> 00:01:28,553
just in app.ts but also in goals.ts so that

36
00:01:28,585 --> 00:01:29,114
this works.

37
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:31,281
And the course goals

38
00:01:31,858 --> 00:01:33,255
should now also be managed there.

39
00:01:33,896 --> 00:01:36,143
So I grab the course goals here and remove

40
00:01:36,143 --> 00:01:37,058
them from app.ts

41
00:01:37,892 --> 00:01:40,684
and instead add them here in the goals.ts

42
00:01:40,684 --> 00:01:42,080
file in the routes folder.

43
00:01:42,642 --> 00:01:44,327
Now with that, we have the routes

44
00:01:44,953 --> 00:01:45,949
in one file

45
00:01:46,719 --> 00:01:49,561
and our core app logic with the remaining

46
00:01:49,834 --> 00:01:52,002
non-routing middleware in another file.

47
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:54,732
Of course, we still need to register our

48
00:01:54,732 --> 00:01:55,952
routes as middleware though,

49
00:01:56,514 --> 00:01:58,842
and therefore in goals.ts, I want to export

50
00:01:58,842 --> 00:02:01,620
that router, and I will export it as the

51
00:02:01,716 --> 00:02:02,262
default

52
00:02:03,402 --> 00:02:05,473
object, as the default export here with

53
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:06,886
export default Router.

54
00:02:07,513 --> 00:02:10,328
And in app.ts, we now need to import it. So

55
00:02:10,328 --> 00:02:12,096
here we can now import our goals

56
00:02:12,686 --> 00:02:13,095
router

57
00:02:13,832 --> 00:02:14,667
from./routes/goals.ts.

58
00:02:19,790 --> 00:02:21,209
You can pick any name you want here,

59
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:24,750
and that's how you import relative to the

60
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:27,161
current file by going into the routes folder

61
00:02:27,275 --> 00:02:28,699
and having a look at goals.ts.

62
00:02:30,619 --> 00:02:32,670
Now we can use the goals router down there

63
00:02:32,719 --> 00:02:33,825
to get access to the routes

64
00:02:34,428 --> 00:02:35,388
and the allowed methods.

65
00:02:38,209 --> 00:02:41,329
We could also outsource the error handling

66
00:02:41,602 --> 00:02:43,436
if we wanted to. I will leave it here though

67
00:02:43,789 --> 00:02:46,105
so that my core middlewares are here, the

68
00:02:46,170 --> 00:02:47,932
dummy middleware and the error handling one.

69
00:02:48,291 --> 00:02:50,168
But you could also outsource that into a

70
00:02:50,168 --> 00:02:51,979
separate file if you wanted to.

71
00:02:53,558 --> 00:02:55,484
I however want to keep the code as it is,

72
00:02:55,921 --> 00:02:57,474
but there still is something I want to do.

73
00:02:58,106 --> 00:03:00,598
I want to put my templates into a folder and

74
00:03:00,679 --> 00:03:02,803
we could name it templates. I will name it

75
00:03:02,883 --> 00:03:03,685
views though

76
00:03:04,247 --> 00:03:06,300
because that's the term you commonly use in

77
00:03:06,412 --> 00:03:07,069
web development.

78
00:03:07,615 --> 00:03:10,261
And I will move the 2 EJS files into the

79
00:03:10,261 --> 00:03:10,919
views folder.

80
00:03:11,945 --> 00:03:13,629
Now with that, of course, we need to update

81
00:03:13,629 --> 00:03:14,463
our paths here

82
00:03:14,992 --> 00:03:19,644
in app.ts. We now import from deno cwd, so

83
00:03:19,644 --> 00:03:21,600
the root working directory here,

84
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:24,503
/views/not-found.ejs.

85
00:03:25,642 --> 00:03:26,973
And in goals, it's the same.

86
00:03:27,583 --> 00:03:28,673
There we also have

87
00:03:29,427 --> 00:03:30,999
/views/course-goals.

88
00:03:31,610 --> 00:03:34,434
It's all relative from the path in which we

89
00:03:34,966 --> 00:03:37,129
execute the Deno command, which will always

90
00:03:37,161 --> 00:03:38,161
be the root folder here.

91
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,511
Now I also wanna put my static files into a

92
00:03:42,511 --> 00:03:45,681
separate folder, so I'll add a static folder

93
00:03:46,376 --> 00:03:48,980
and move app.css into that static folder.

94
00:03:49,514 --> 00:03:51,476
With that CSS file moved though,

95
00:03:52,087 --> 00:03:54,418
we have to keep in mind that in course

96
00:03:54,418 --> 00:03:54,724
goals,

97
00:03:55,383 --> 00:03:57,891
I do import just app.css like this.

98
00:03:58,644 --> 00:04:00,322
We now need to update this to

99
00:04:00,322 --> 00:04:04,194
/static/app.css for this to work because

100
00:04:04,194 --> 00:04:06,679
otherwise it will look for just app.css, but

101
00:04:06,776 --> 00:04:08,602
this file like that does not exist anymore.

102
00:04:08,894 --> 00:04:11,878
A path of just app.css in the root folder of

103
00:04:11,878 --> 00:04:13,905
the project doesn't exist anymore.

104
00:04:14,894 --> 00:04:16,127
With that all, if we go back,

105
00:04:18,090 --> 00:04:18,752
we can reload

106
00:04:20,043 --> 00:04:22,449
and the application still works just fine

107
00:04:23,757 --> 00:04:24,467
as you can tell.

108
00:04:25,457 --> 00:04:26,322
However, there's one

109
00:04:27,156 --> 00:04:29,944
alternative to having the static app.css

110
00:04:29,944 --> 00:04:30,714
file like this here.

111
00:04:31,403 --> 00:04:32,861
You could also remove that here

112
00:04:33,631 --> 00:04:35,458
and just point at app.css,

113
00:04:36,596 --> 00:04:38,134
and therefore it would not work.

114
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:42,414
But then go to your send function and there

115
00:04:42,462 --> 00:04:45,106
pass in a 3rd argument, which is an object

116
00:04:45,106 --> 00:04:46,917
that allows you to configure that send

117
00:04:46,933 --> 00:04:47,334
function.

118
00:04:48,232 --> 00:04:48,504
And there

119
00:04:49,354 --> 00:04:51,726
you can set the root directory to a

120
00:04:51,838 --> 00:04:53,569
different directory than it would normally

121
00:04:53,665 --> 00:04:53,761
be.

122
00:04:54,393 --> 00:04:56,882
Normally it takes your project root as the

123
00:04:56,882 --> 00:04:59,210
root directory, which means that if we're

124
00:04:59,226 --> 00:05:01,812
requesting app.css like this, it will look

125
00:05:01,828 --> 00:05:03,089
for it in the root folder.

126
00:05:03,843 --> 00:05:05,533
We can change that. We could say that the

127
00:05:05,614 --> 00:05:07,547
root folder is actually

128
00:05:08,149 --> 00:05:09,351
static so

129
00:05:10,550 --> 00:05:12,737
that it should take that static folder as

130
00:05:12,754 --> 00:05:13,434
the root folder.

131
00:05:14,002 --> 00:05:16,643
Now it will look for app.css in the static

132
00:05:16,643 --> 00:05:19,479
folder automatically. Hence, if we save that

133
00:05:19,479 --> 00:05:19,949
and reload

134
00:05:21,315 --> 00:05:24,017
we got our styles back even though we're

135
00:05:24,017 --> 00:05:26,218
still importing just app.css here.

136
00:05:26,995 --> 00:05:29,148
So that simply is an alternative to updating

137
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:31,377
the import path here in the template. You

138
00:05:31,377 --> 00:05:34,150
can either update it here or set a different

139
00:05:34,166 --> 00:05:36,650
root folder here, whatever you personally

140
00:05:36,762 --> 00:05:37,166
prefer.

141
00:05:38,992 --> 00:05:42,671
And with that, we have all the core features

142
00:05:42,865 --> 00:05:46,012
that you need to have in mind about Oak

143
00:05:46,422 --> 00:05:47,160
covered. We

144
00:05:47,769 --> 00:05:50,239
had a close look at all the core essentials

145
00:05:50,271 --> 00:05:52,789
that make up Oak, and you can hopefully see

146
00:05:52,998 --> 00:05:56,494
that building real web apps is way more fun

147
00:05:56,751 --> 00:05:59,397
and realistic with a framework like Oak

148
00:05:59,718 --> 00:06:01,690
because we can really focus on our core

149
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:04,914
business logic. We can have the HTML code in

150
00:06:05,010 --> 00:06:07,817
a standalone file, and we don't have to do

151
00:06:08,057 --> 00:06:10,784
all the low-level wiring up with Deno

152
00:06:10,864 --> 00:06:11,281
itself.

153
00:06:11,939 --> 00:06:14,168
So that's the route which will continue over

154
00:06:14,168 --> 00:06:15,098
the next modules.
